From 5e7d3348447abe9900d3d6c59649b92d944fc594 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: wivi514 <wivi514@hotmail.com>
Date: Mon, 3 Aug 2026 16:10:49 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 07/14] ppc_context: guard PPC_FUNC_PROLOGUE with #ifndef

Every emitted function body opens with PPC_FUNC_PROLOGUE(), which makes it the
one place a port can attach whole-image, per-function instrumentation. The weak
alias seam only covers functions you thought to hook, and a PPC_CALL_INDIRECT_FUNC
hook cannot see direct or tail calls, so neither can answer 'which guest functions
did this run execute, and in what order'. That question turns a Xenia
--trace_function_data capture into a control-flow divergence oracle.

Guarded the same way PPC_LOAD_*/PPC_CALL_INDIRECT_FUNC already are, so a
force-included header can define its own and paste the __builtin_assume back in.
No behaviour change when nothing overrides it.
---
 XenonUtils/ppc_context.h | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/XenonUtils/ppc_context.h b/XenonUtils/ppc_context.h
index c0841fe..777e9ff 100644
--- a/XenonUtils/ppc_context.h
+++ b/XenonUtils/ppc_context.h
@@ -29,7 +29,15 @@
 #define PPC_EXTERN_FUNC(x) extern PPC_FUNC(x)
 #define PPC_WEAK_FUNC(x) __attribute__((weak,noinline)) PPC_FUNC(x)
 
+// Guarded like PPC_LOAD_*/PPC_CALL_INDIRECT_FUNC below, so a port can force-include a
+// header that defines its own prologue and still get this one's __builtin_assume by
+// pasting it in. Every emitted function body opens with this macro, which makes it the
+// only place a port can attach whole-image, per-function instrumentation that cannot be
+// bypassed: the weak-alias seam covers only functions you thought to hook, and an
+// indirect-call hook cannot see a direct or tail call.
+#ifndef PPC_FUNC_PROLOGUE
 #define PPC_FUNC_PROLOGUE() __builtin_assume(((size_t)base & 0x1F) == 0)
+#endif
 
 #ifndef PPC_LOAD_U8
 #define PPC_LOAD_U8(x) *(volatile uint8_t*)(base + (x))
